const COVER=[["Codification Portal",46,34],["Search service",18,16],["Taxonomy API",9,5],["Contract Repository",21,13],["Lease subledger (ERP)",15,6],["Entra ID",31,24],["M365",12,5]];
const HEAT={topics:TOPICS,auds:["Public","Editors","Service desk","Finance","Vendors","Executives"],m:[[90,70,88,0,0,40],[0,66,82,0,34,0],[0,20,25,52,0,48],[20,55,40,60,0,35],[0,72,90,0,30,45],[35,48,60,0,28,0],[0,0,40,0,18,70]]};
const SUGGEST=[{id:"s1",t:"A later save cancels a scheduled publish",ev:"9 searches this week · 3 incidents (INC0102, INC0089, INC0074)",src:"INC0102",conf:.88},{id:"s2",t:"Vendor laptops lose VPN every 10 minutes",ev:"14 searches · INC0105 closed with a clear fix",src:"INC0105",conf:.84},{id:"s3",t:"Export the lease schedule after the ERP upgrade",ev:"11 searches by Finance · INC0091 · KB0201 retired with no replacement",src:"INC0091",conf:.9},{id:"s4",t:"Who approves taxonomy term changes",ev:"8 searches, no incident. Needs an owner to write it",src:null,conf:.52},{id:"s5",t:"Portal slow: the first 15 minutes",ev:"Daily ops meeting Oct 6 · 41 'portal slow' searches with no click",src:"m3",conf:.74}];
function gapDraft(sg){const src=sg.src?srcOf(sg.src):null;K.ed=blank();if(src){K.aiSrc=src.id;applyDraft(src)}else{K.ed.t=sg.t;K.ed.s.sym=sg.t+"?";toast("No source to cite yet. A blank draft is open for the owner to write.","info")}
 audit("drafted article from gap",sg.t);go("kcs_edit")}
function applyDraft(src){const d=src.d,e=K.ed;e.t=d.t;e.type=d.type;e.aud=d.aud.slice();e.cls=d.cls;e.svc=d.svc;e.topic=d.topic;e.s=Object.assign({},d.s);e.srcs=[src.id+" "+src.k.toLowerCase()];e.ai={};e.cites=d.cites;Object.keys(d.cites).forEach(k=>e.ai[k]=true);e.aiSrc=src.id;e.aiConf=d.conf;e.rvw="Nia Brooks";e.own="Maya Ortiz"}
function heatCell(v,t,a){const cls=v>=70?"good":v>=40?"warn":v>0?"bad":"none";return `<button class="kcs-hc ${cls}" data-kcs-heat="${t}:${a}" title="${v}% of searches answered"><b data-role="metric">${v?v+"%":"none"}</b></button>`}
REG("kcs_gap","Knowledge gaps and analytics","know","M4 20V10M10 20V4M16 20v-7M22 20H2",()=>{
 const un=K.gaps.map(g=>({q:g.q,n:g.n,aud:g.aud,last:g.last,top:"New (from Ask)",live:1,draft:g.draft})).concat(UNANS);const totU=un.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.n,0);const low=pub().filter(a=>a.help&&a.help<70).sort((a,b)=>a.help-b.help);
 const cov=COVER.map(c=>({s:c[0],i:c[1],c:c[2],p:Math.round(100*c[2]/c[1])}));const wc=Math.round(100*cov.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.c,0)/cov.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.i,0));const worst=cov.slice().sort((a,b)=>a.p-b.p)[0];
 return `<div class="screen">${hero("Knowledge gaps and analytics","Find what people need that we have not written",`People asked <b>${totU} questions</b> this month that no published article answered. The biggest is <b>${esc(un[0].q)}</b>. Coverage is weakest for <b>${esc(worst.s)}</b>: only <b>${worst.p}%</b> of its incidents have a linked article.`,`<div class="row">${fchip("m_deflect_kb")}${fchip("m_kbfresh")}<button class="btn primary" data-kcs-draftall>Draft top 3 with AI</button></div>`)}${lensNote()}
 ${tiles([TL("Unanswered searches",totU,un.length+" distinct questions",totU>60?"bad":"warn"),TL("Searches with no click","152","5 queries led nowhere","warn"),TL("Low helpfulness",low.length,"articles under 70% helpful",low.length?"warn":"good"),TL("Incident coverage",wc+"%","incidents with a linked article",wc>=70?"good":"warn")])}
 <div class="grid g2"><section class="card glass"><div class="cardhead"><div><h3>Top unanswered searches</h3><span class="muted small" data-role="story">The question was asked and the knowledge base said it could not answer.</span></div></div><div class="kcs-list">${un.slice(0,8).map(x=>`<div class="kcs-li"><div><b>${esc(x.q)}</b>${x.live?" "+pill("new","info"):""}<span class="muted small">${esc(x.aud)} · last ${x.last} · ${esc(x.top)}</span></div><div class="row" style="gap:8px;flex-wrap:nowrap"><b class="num" data-role="metric" style="font-size:22px">${x.n}</b>${x.draft?`<button class="btn" data-kcs-open="${x.draft}">Draft exists</button>`:`<button class="btn" data-kcs-gapdraft="${esc(x.q)}">Draft it</button>`}</div></div>`).join("")}</div></section>
 <section class="card glass"><div class="cardhead"><div><h3>Searches with no click</h3><span class="muted small" data-role="story">Results appeared and nobody opened one: the titles or ranking are wrong.</span></div></div><div class="kcs-list">${NOCLICK.map(x=>`<div class="kcs-li"><div><b>${esc(x.q)}</b><span class="muted small">${esc(x.why)}</span></div><div class="row" style="gap:8px;flex-wrap:nowrap"><span class="pill ${x.rate>=55?"bad":"warn"}" data-role="metric">${x.rate}% no click</span><b class="num" data-role="metric">${x.n}</b></div></div>`).join("")}</div>
 <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:8px">No-click rate = searches with results and zero result clicks ÷ searches with results.</p></section></div>
 <div class="grid g2"><section class="card glass"><div class="cardhead"><div><h3>Low helpfulness</h3><span class="muted small">Published articles people mark as not helpful.</span></div></div>${low.length?`<div class="kcs-list">${low.map(a=>`<div class="kcs-li" data-kcs-open="${a.id}" tabindex="0"><div><b>${esc(a.t)}</b><span class="muted small">${a.id} · ${a.views} views · ${esc(a.own)}</span></div><span class="pill ${a.help<55?"bad":"warn"}" data-role="metric">${a.help}% helpful</span></div>`).join("")}</div>`:empty("None","Every published article is at least 70% helpful.")}<p class="muted small" style="margin-top:8px">Helpfulness = helpful votes ÷ all votes. Articles under 70% go to their owner with the comments.</p></section>
 <section class="card glass"><div class="cardhead"><div><h3>Coverage by service</h3><span class="muted small" data-role="story">Incidents closed in 90 days that carry a linked article.</span></div></div><div class="kcs-bars">${cov.map(c=>`<div class="kcs-br"><span class="kcs-bl">${esc(c.s)}</span><span class="kcs-bt"><i style="width:${c.p}%;background:var(--${c.p>=70?"good":c.p>=50?"warn":"bad"}-f)"></i></span><b class="num" data-role="metric">${c.p}%</b></div>`).join("")}</div><div class="formula" style="margin-top:10px;font-size:15px">Coverage = incidents with a linked article ÷ incidents closed</div></section></div>
 <section class="card glass"><div class="cardhead"><div><h3>Suggested new articles</h3><span class="muted small" data-role="story">Ranked by searches plus incidents. Each draft cites its evidence and still needs a human editor and a reviewer.</span></div></div><div class="grid g3">${SUGGEST.map(s=>`<div class="tile glass kcs-sg ${K.done&&K.done[s.id]?"done":""}"><div class="row sp">${aiChip({model:"Claude Sonnet",conf:s.conf,title:"Why this is suggested",note:s.ev,src:[s.ev],guards:["Draft only","Cites its sources"]})}</div><b>${esc(s.t)}</b><span class="muted small">${esc(s.ev)}</span><button class="btn primary" data-kcs-draftit="${s.id}">${K.done&&K.done[s.id]?"Drafted: open again":"Draft it"}</button></div>`).join("")}</div></section>
 <div class="grid g2"><section class="card glass"><div class="cardhead"><div><h3>Coverage heat grid</h3><span class="muted small" data-role="story">Share of searches answered, by topic and audience. Blank means nobody has searched or no article is visible.</span></div></div><div class="tablewrap" style="max-height:none"><div class="kcs-heat" style="--n:${HEAT.auds.length}"><span></span>${HEAT.auds.map(a=>`<span class="kcs-hh">${a}</span>`).join("")}${HEAT.topics.map((t,i)=>`<span class="kcs-ht">${t}</span>${HEAT.auds.map((a,j)=>heatCell(HEAT.m[i][j],i,j)).join("")}`).join("")}</div></div><div class="row small muted" style="margin-top:8px"><span class="pill good">70% and up</span><span class="pill warn">40 to 69%</span><span class="pill bad">under 40%</span><span class="pill mute">none</span></div></section>
 <section class="card glass"><div class="cardhead"><div><h3>How each number is calculated</h3></div></div><dl class="kv" style="grid-template-columns:120px 1fr"><dt>Unanswered</dt><dd>Questions where retrieval scored under 0.34, or every match was filtered by permission.</dd><dt>No click</dt><dd>Searches with results and no click ÷ searches with results.</dd><dt>Helpfulness</dt><dd>Helpful votes ÷ votes.</dd><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>Incidents with a linked article ÷ incidents closed.</dd><dt>Heat cell</dt><dd>Searches answered by a published article visible to that audience ÷ searches by that audience on that topic.</dd><dt>Deflection</dt><dd>${esc(METRICS.m_deflect_kb.f)}</dd></dl><div class="row">${fchip("m_deflect_kb")}${fchip("m_kbfresh")}${fchip("m_ground")}</div></section></div></div>`});

/* ---------- Prompt library ---------- */
const rp=(t,e)=>e.reduce((s,x)=>s.replace(x[1],x[0]),t);
const V=(v,d,by,note,text,sc,st)=>({v,d,by,note,text,sc,st:st||"retired"});
const B101=`You answer questions for Meridian Standards Foundation staff using only the context chunks below.
Rules:
1. Use only facts that appear in the chunks. Never use outside knowledge.
2. Cite every sentence with the chunk number in square brackets, for example [1].
3. If the chunks do not contain the answer, reply exactly: "I could not find this in the knowledge base." and stop.
4. The reader belongs to these groups: {{viewer_groups}}. Never mention content from other groups.
5. If a cited article was last reviewed more than 12 months ago, say so in one sentence.
Question: {{question}}
Context chunks:
{{chunks}}`;
